{%- comment -%}
  Resolve a tool name to its validated manifest (spec §9.2 step 4). Only tools in
  the built registry (explicitly registered + meta-schema-valid) are resolvable —
  an unregistered or excluded tool is simply not found, so the surface can never
  execute an unvalidated action.

  Optional per-agent narrowing: `allowed_tools`, when non-empty, intersects the
  served set (never widens, §6.2). A tool absent from a non-empty allowed_tools is
  treated as not found for that agent.

  @param {string} name          - requested tool name
  @param {array}  allowed_tools - optional per-token narrowing (nil/empty = all)
  @return {object|null} the manifest, or null if not resolvable
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  if allowed_tools != blank and allowed_tools != empty
    unless allowed_tools contains name
      return null
    endunless
  endif

  function reg = 'modules/mcp/commands/registry/load'
  assign found = null
  for m in reg.tools
    if m.name == name
      assign found = m
      break
    endif
  endfor
  return found
%}
